---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  description={`The terms for using the ${site.name} website.`}
  lede="The short rules for using this website. Client work is covered by a separate written agreement."
>
  <h2>What these terms cover</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of this website, which is run by {site.legalEntity}, doing business as {site.name}, of
    {site.legalAddress}. They don't cover work we do for clients. That is always set out in a separate agreement signed by both sides.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    You're welcome to read, link to and share anything here. Please don't try to break the site, scrape it in a way
    that strains it, or use it to send us anything unlawful.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The words, design and code on this site belong to {site.legalEntity} unless we say otherwise. You may quote from
    our articles with a link back to the original.
  </p>

  <h2>Articles are general information</h2>
  <p>
    Our insights are written in good faith from our own experience. They aren't advice about your specific situation,
    and you shouldn't rely on them as such. If you want advice for your business, talk to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Descriptions of our services</h2>
  <p>
    Service descriptions, timeframes and prices on this site describe how we normally work. The terms of any actual
    engagement are the ones in the agreement we sign with you.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Where we link to other websites, we aren't responsible for what's on them.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    This website is provided as is. To the extent the law allows, {site.legalEntity} isn't liable for any loss arising
    from your use of the site or reliance on its content.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the law of {site.jurisdiction}.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or {site.phoneDisplay}.
  </p>
</Legal>
